WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.410
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:36.910
Valon, you were my enemy, but you were also a great duelist.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:44.530
Mai, I won't even let you disparage our duel since we gave it our all.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.720
Bring it on, Mai.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.500
If we can only understand each other by dueling, I won't run away!

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.680
I'll duel you with all my strength!

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:01.730
Bitter Victory

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:10.040
Jonouchi!  Where are you?

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.480
Jonouchi!

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.150
Jonouchi!

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:19.210
Damn!  The Seal appeared somewhere around here!

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.170
I’m sure we’re close.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.820
Don’t give up!  Let’s find him!

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:24.220
Yeah.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.400
All these weaklings.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.770
Come, Blue-Eyes!

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.130
Destroy these weaklings!

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.770
Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.730
Where do they come from?

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.960
There's more of them, big brother!

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.120
No matter how many, the weak are still weak.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.720
They're no match for me.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.650
Go, Blue-Eyes!

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.560
Big brother!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.540
Mokuba!  How dare you!

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.720
Come out, Critias!

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:36.200
Mokuba!

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:36.930
Big brother!

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:40.860
There's no end to these weaklings!

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.140
Blue-Eyes!  Critias!

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.140
Destroy everything!

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.830
My turn.  I draw!

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.190
I summon Swordsman of Landstar in defense position!

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:15.250
I set two cards-

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.940
I set two cards... and end my turn...

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.250
My eyes are getting blurry.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.280
The damage I took was huge.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.560
But this isn’t the end!

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:47.240
You talk a big game, but you're only defending.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.670
For now.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.460
You never change.

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:58.680
Even against stronger opponents or in dire situations, you never give up.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.480
Aren’t you scared of losing?

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:05.000
Then let me ask you.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.420
What does winning mean to you?

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:11.130
Just defeat someone in a duel?

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:12.860
Umm…

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:18.060
You used to say that you couldn't trust anyone.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:20.300
That you could only trust yourself.

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:28.610
But by fighting together at Duelist Kingdom, we found something more important than winning.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:37.650
So why did you revert back to when you fought alone?

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:43.260
I’ve always been alone.  Always!

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.260
You're wrong!  You're my friend!

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.190
Even now!

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.540
It’s too late!

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.630
I have to keep fighting!

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.560
Mai...

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.580
I've heard enough of your nonsense!

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.000
I'll defeat you, and that's it!

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.180
Mai...

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:08.010
No.  I still believe how you were, and I'll understand how you feel!

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.110
Bring it, Mai!

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:12.780
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.090
Harpie Lady attacks Swordsman of Landstar!

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.190
Now!  I flip over my set card!

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.100
Double Magical Arm Bind!

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:31.800
By tributing two of my monsters, this trap lets me control two of your monsters!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.410
But I still have Harpies!

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.840
Attack!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.740
Hold up!  I have another card!

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.610
I flip over my set card!

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.720
Vow of Tribe!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:51.120
On the turn it activates, the same monsters can’t battle each other!

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.940
Since I have Harpie Ladies on my field, you can't attack this turn.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.520
This battle is over.

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.570
Not bad.

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:05.080
With every duel, I’m improving bit by bit.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.500
That’s how I came this far.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.900
His willpower is his strength.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:16.580
No matter how bad he's beaten, he never gives up.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.020
That's what I don't have.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:24.690
I finally know why you're obsessed with Jonouchi.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.230
He has something we don’t have.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:32.230
And that attracts you.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:37.400
His pure passion towards dueling.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.840
I really don't have that?

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:46.510
Then I'll gain true power when I defeat you!

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.030
The strength to never lose!

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.720
I end my turn!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:13.390
Mai, I sense the soul of a duelist within you.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:18.910
Your excitement to duel, regardless of Doma.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:24.910
Then as a duelist, I'll fight you with all my strength to the end!

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.080
My turn!

00:08:26.490 --> 00:08:27.250
I draw!

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:34.210
I tribute two Harpie Ladies and Swordsman of Landstar!

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.130
Three tributes?

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:40.530
Come out!  Gilford the Lightning!

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:54.050
When I tribute three monsters to summon Gilford the Lightning…

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.850
All monsters on your field are destroyed!

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:09.660
Gilford the Lightning attacks you directly!

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:24.960
Get up, Mai!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.510
Our duel isn’t over yet!

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.460
You’ve certainly become stronger, Jonouchi.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:39.520
But I'll still win!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.120
I end my turn!

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.880
Then here I go!

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.120
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:11.560
Card of Sanctity!

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:16.160
We both draw until we have six cards in our hands!

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.600
You draw too, Jonouchi.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:19.650
Yeah.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.940
Did you draw that card?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.600
Maybe, maybe not.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.460
I didn't draw Hermos, but I drew good cards.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:37.890
Even if he drew Hermos, I’ll attack before he can use it!

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.980
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.120
Monster Reborn!

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.860
Resurrect, Harpie Lady!

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.380
Here's another spell card!

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:53.090
I activate Elegant Egotist!

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:58.670
It duplicates and Special Summons my Harpies!

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.400
She instantly summoned three monsters!

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:10.190
No way...  That can't be...

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.280
Yes.

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:12.750
Here I go, Jonouchi!

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:16.070
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.070
Harpie Lady Phoenix Formation!

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:26.600
For every Harpie on the field, Phoenix Formation destroy your monster.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:33.170
And you take damage equal to the destroyed monsters’ total attack points!

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.610
Go, Harpie Ladies!

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.150
That hurt.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:56.590
How’s that?  My Harpie combo is invincible!

00:11:57.180 --> 00:11:59.590
Impressive, Mai.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:02.530
You damaged my life points.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.540
You still have the strength to talk?

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:06.980
You're tough.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:11.970
It'd be a waste to let a duel against you end quickly.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:15.950
I think you're a true duelist.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:19.050
So I can fight you with all my strength.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.860
What's more fun than this?

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:25.990
I end my turn!

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.680
My turn.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:31.990
Damn...  Just hold on...

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.430
For Mai!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.300
I draw!

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:45.040
Hermos!  Give me your remaining power!

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.130
I activate the spell card, The Warrior Returning Alive!

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:54.780
It returns a Warrior-Type monster in the graveyard to my hand!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.420
I summon Blue Flame Swordsman in attack position!

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:03.340
I activate a Ritual Spell from my hand!

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:05.050
Dark Dragon Ritual!

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:09.770
A Ritual Spell?

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:14.040
I tribute Gearfried the Iron Knight from my hand!

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.700
I summon Knight of Dark Dragon!

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:22.310
It activate its effect!

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:26.220
By tributing Knight of Dark Dragon...

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:33.260
...I can Special Summon Red-Eyes B. Dragon from my deck or my hand!

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:35.950
Come out, Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:42.570
But when that effect summons it, it can't attack this turn!

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:47.640
I know.  That’s why I’m activating this from my hand!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.580
Claw of Hermos!

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.210
I fuse Red-Eyes and Hermos!

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:02.250
Red-Eyes B. Dragon Sword!

00:14:02.720 --> 00:14:04.690
I equip it on Blue Flame Swordsman!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.620
It gains 1000 attack points!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.620
Go, Blue Flame Swordsman!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.130
Attack Harpie Lady!

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:22.640
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.740
No.  Not yet.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.050
I'm almost there.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:34.270
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:38.320
It doesn't matter if that Equip Card is strong if I destroy it!

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:39.030
What?

00:14:39.030 --> 00:14:41.440
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.240
Harpie's Feather Duster!

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:53.300
If I attack, I can destroy Blue Flame Swordsman.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:56.480
And Jonouchi if I attack him directly.

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:03.340
Since you’ve come this far, I'll crush you with all my might.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:06.280
The spell card, Spell Reproduction!

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:10.990
By sending two spell cards in my hand to my graveyard...

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:15.090
...I can add a spell card in my graveyard to my hand!

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:20.030
The card she'd want to get back would be... Phoenix Formation!

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:24.470
Yes.  I'll use all my strength to defeat you!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:27.500
Harpie Lady Phoenix Formation!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:32.510
You lose life points equal to the destroyed monster's attack points!

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:36.480
What?  0 attack points?

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:40.860
I activated Blue Flame Swordsman’s effect.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:45.890
Blue Flame Swordsman can transfer its attack points to another monster.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:48.890
It gave its attack points to my Harpie?

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.330
Yeah.  All of it.

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.330
Blue Flame Swordsman has 0 attack points.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.690
So I take 0 damage.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:02.930
And when Blue Flame Swordsman is destroyed, I can Special Summon Flame Swordsman!

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:09.200
You'd give attack points to my monster in order to survive this turn?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.950
What are you thinking?

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.290
You want to call me an idiot.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.730
And I'd agree.

00:16:15.730 --> 00:16:18.890
But this is the best I can do.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:24.890
With this duel, I want you to remember something important.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:28.690
You're strong enough to fight on your own!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:32.130
Even without Doma’s help!

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:37.070
I know you're actually a kind person.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:43.600
Come to think of it, I never paid back my debt.

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:51.390
You're trying to confuse me, but it won't work!

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.580
No, I’m not!

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:56.720
Act for yourself, Mai!

00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:01.530
Or you’ll keep suffering forever!

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.940
Mai...

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:11.760
I can’t go back.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.950
This is my path.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:15.680
I end my turn!

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:19.220
My turn.  I draw.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:25.160
I set a card.

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:27.410
I end... my turn...

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:34.220
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:38.900
Cyber Harpie attacks Flame Swordsman!

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.070
This is the end, Jonouchi!

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.440
I flip over my set card.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.560
Skull Dice!

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:58.830
Harpie Lady's attack points are halved!

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:00.720
I'm still going to win!

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:07.090
When my Harpie Lady attacks you directly, you'll lose!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:11.400
Harpie, attack Jonouchi-

00:18:16.130 --> 00:18:17.340
Why?

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.630
Why am I hesitating?

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.780
With this, I'll win.

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.700
You win, Mai.

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.380
Jonouchi!

00:19:04.650 --> 00:19:05.800
Jonouchi!

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.390
Valon's duel already wore you out.

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.330
Sorry.  I can’t see your face anymore.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:15.930
You dueled me in this condition?

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:21.900
Sorry.  I couldn’t do anything for you.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:27.170
But I’m glad they didn't steal your soul.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:29.020
Jonouchi!

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:33.310
This duel was fun.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.200
No!

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:47.260
Here it comes.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.640
Mai Kujaku won, but…

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.140
Yugi?

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:01.530
Timaeus.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:16.460
Critias is howling.

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:19.890
Jonouchi!

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:21.790
No!

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.760
No, Jonouchi!

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:30.370
I knew all along that winning like this wouldn't help.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:34.530
I knew all along...

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:38.320
I’m such a fool.

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:45.200
What could I get by sacrificing you?

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:54.030
Dartz!  I’ll make you pay for this!

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:00.620
Just wait, Jonouchi and Valon.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.870
I'll get your souls back!

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:31.810
You’re…

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:39.860
No way...

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:41.290
It can’t be…

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:43.700
Jonouchi...

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:06.920
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:15.290
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:26.450
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:27.060 --> 00:22:35.940
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:45.000
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:50.510
I'll live feeling them

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:55.660
For me to be me

00:22:55.660 --> 00:23:04.150
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:04.830 --> 00:23:09.790
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:10.310 --> 00:23:19.450
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:28.000
Jonouchi lost?  You must be joking!

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:34.020
But if Valon is also unconscious, does that mean Mai stole Jonouchi's soul?

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:36.370
I can't believe it!

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:39.930
With pain in his heart, Yugi enters Paradius alone.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.780
Yugi sees Mai with her soul stolen.

00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:47.000
Who did that?

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.970
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Duel of Destiny!
Yugi vs Rafael

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:52.720
Duel, standby!
